municating ideas\", \"regarded as egocentric\", \"not willing to further his education\". We can argue that communication can be trained, egocentric may be mitigated, lack of further education is less critical for pilot role.\n\nThus we can propose Candidate C as provisional recommendation, challenging James's B. Provide reasoning.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I appreciate James's points, but I think Candidate C's decision quality and calmness under pressure are more critical, and his concern for others suggests good crew cooperation, outweighing communication issues.\" Vote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
