's communication issues are concerning but can be mitigated. He may decide to shift his vote to C, aligning with others, or stay with B if he believes B's strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nGiven the panel is leaning to C, James should consider if any new evidence changes his view. He might argue that B's weak numeric memory is a serious safety risk, and nasty remarks are a crew cooperation issue, while C's strengths are more critical. He could shift his vote to C.\n\nThus James should state his current recommendation (maybe now Candidate C) and explain why he changes: B's memory and remarks are more severe than C's communication issues, and C's decision quality and calmness are vital. Also note D's issues.\n\nHe should reference explicit facts: B weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks; C can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything; D's arrogance, hot temper.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
